<section id="method">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">Method</div>
    <h2>I read systems as texts.</h2>
    <p class="section-copy">
      My first formation was literary: not paraphrase, not summary, but reading what a text hides,
      assumes, displaces, and forces the reader to infer.
    </p>
    <p class="section-copy">
      That became a method for reading systems.
    </p>
    <div class="text-list">
      <span>A SaaS flow is a text.</span>
      <span>A form is a text.</span>
      <span>An AI workflow is a text.</span>
      <span>A classroom is a text.</span>
      <span>A video is a text.</span>
      <span>A support pattern is a text.</span>
    </div>
    <p class="section-copy">
      I combine literature, pedagogy, qualitative research, behavioral reading, and web systems development
      to identify the scaffold a system assumes but never designed.
    </p>
    <div class="method-note">
      When the system stops guiding, the real design begins.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
